/* Changelog, newest first: [date, text] or [date, text, "wiki"]. Tag game-data changes picked up from the wiki
   (the daily wiki check) with "wiki" so they show under Site changes > Wiki updates. */
ARC.DATA_CHANGES = [
    ["Oct 27, 2026", "Translated the newest parts of the site into all 7 other languages: the Stash cards and tiles (Want, Keep, Sell, Looking for, slots, Sell it anyway), Your best gun on enemy cards, the QR transfer and its messages, and the phone tab bar picker."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Move your settings between phone and PC with a QR code: Home > Back up or move your data > Show QR code. Scan it with the other device and your Wants, tags, notes, favourites, starred conditions and keys are added there, without replacing what is already on it."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Daily check: the Bully card now lists its full loot from the wiki (12 drops, including ARC Coolant, ARC Motion Core and Launcher Ammo), its 2,000 to 4,000 health and all four Pendola Pass spots. The Hydra card now lists its drops: Light Ammo, ARC Powercell and ARC Alloy.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Enemy cards in Reference now show \"Your best gun\": the weapon in your Stash that kills that enemy fastest, with body hits, time and how it handles the armor. It uses the same numbers as Shots to kill."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Enemy cards now list the maps the wiki gives for the Queen and the Matriarch (Dam Battlegrounds, Spaceport and The Blue Gate, through their map conditions), and the Shredder card notes it is no longer only on Stella Montis. The wiki names no maps for the other enemies.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "The Stash no longer calls your weapons, augments and shields safe to sell: they count as Keep, and a \"Sell it anyway\" button on the card moves one to Sell. The spare-items total on Home skips them too."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Search everything now finds blueprints when you type the word: \"anvil blueprint\" goes straight to the Anvil blueprint, and \"blueprint\" on its own lists them."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Added the 15 Amplified weapons (Amplified Hairpin to Amplified Jupiter) with how to make each one and its amplification paths, so ARC Tracker sync matches them. No sell price is published for them yet, on the wiki or anywhere else."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "New on phones: choose which tabs sit in the bottom bar. Open More, tap Choose bar tabs and pick up to 5. The rest stay under More."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Stash tab: the Looking for tile now shows how many slots the items you are still looking for take at their Want amounts. Items you already have enough of are left out of it, the same as in the Looking for filter."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "Filled in data gaps: where to find 202 items (blueprints, trinkets and quest items from the item data, weapon upgrade steps for Canto II to IV, and Amplified Fragments, which come from recycling an Amplified weapon). Keys now count their source from the Keys list. The wiki has no sell price yet for ARC Plated Coupler, Banjo, Bantam III and IV, Propellant Valve Assembly or Stiletto III.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync now counts weapons. ARC Tracker puts the attached mod in a weapon's name (like Bettina IV · Extended Mag), so they were skipped before. Weapon versions this site does not list yet, like Amplified Bettina, show under their own name."],
    ["Oct 26, 2026", "The Tools tab is gone. The tools other pages linked to moved there: Quest route planner, Weekly goals and Workshop planner on Home, Crafting planner in the item lookup, Raid log on Raids and Shots to kill in Reference. The rest were removed."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Stash tab: a new Looking for tile shows how many more slots you need to reach your Want amounts. The Stash space planner tool was removed."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Stash: the Looking for filter now only shows items you still need more of, and hides the ones that already reached your Want amount."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync now brings in ammo and every other item the game data lists (trinkets, quest items and more), with prices and stack sizes, so your Stash matches ARC Tracker."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Added 4 Emperor drops used to craft amplified weapons: Fluted Rotor Core, Pneumatic Actuator, Pressure Regulator and Propellant Valve Assembly."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Fixed: Stash slot count. Amplified Fragments now stack to 50 (they were counted as 1 slot each), and right after a sync the site shows ARC Tracker's own slot count."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Fixed: ARC Tracker sync now removes items you no longer have from your Stash, even when ARC Tracker lists something the site doesn't know yet."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "New shareable summary page for every game update, with post text ready to copy for Reddit, Discord or video descriptions. Open one from Update history (\"Summary page to share\") or the Game updates list."],
    ["Oct 25, 2026", "Daily check: Trials moved to Season 6 Week 3 (Oct 20 to 26). Hydra now shows its health (1050), XP (500, plus 500 for its core and 400 for its turret), weaker back plating, and that it also sits inside the Emperor.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 24, 2026", "Daily check: trader stock refreshed from the wiki. Apollo now sells Dockmaster's Detector, Shrapnel, Tagging, Trigger 'Nade, Heavy Fuze and Blaze grenades and the Surge Coil, and no longer the Gas Mine or Jolt Mine. Lance now sells the three Mk. 3 augments (Cautious, Flanking, Healing). Old Shani Cred listings removed from Mk. 2 augments, Sterilized Bandage, Surge Shield Recharger and Extended Light Mag II.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 23, 2026", "Daily check: the Matriarch now also drops the ARC Insulated Coupler, per the wiki.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 22, 2026", "Daily check: Snap Hook now recycles into 1 Power Rod and 2 Steel Cable (was 3 Rope), per the wiki.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 20, 2026", "Daily check: added Apollo's two new hidden quests, Nothing Ventured (Comets, Rocketeers and Sentinels; rewards Deadline, Wolfpack and a bonus Deadline Blueprint) and Nothing Gained (a Queen and a Matriarch; rewards their reactors and Bettina III).", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 18, 2026", "New Where to farm section at the bottom of the Maps tab: every item the wiki gives a location for, with its best map, ARC drops, traders and quest rewards. Search it or filter to what your stash still needs, and open an item for the matching spots on each map."],
    ["Oct 18, 2026", "New raid calendar in the Raids tab: a month view with each day colored green or red by that day's profit, plus the month's best and worst days. Tap a day to see just its raids."],
    ["Oct 17, 2026", "Fixed the Home card sizing: cards now fit their content and stack neatly in columns, with no big empty gaps or stretched buttons."],
    ["Oct 17, 2026", "New stash worth chart on the Home Stash card: your stash value day by day for up to 90 days, with how much it changed over the last 7 days and overall. It uses the daily snapshots the site already keeps, so it starts with your past days, each valued at today's sell prices."],
    ["Oct 17, 2026", "New Customize Home at the bottom of Home: untick a card to hide it (including the stat tiles) and use the arrows to move cards up or down. Your layout is saved in this browser, and Back to the default layout undoes it."],
    ["Oct 17, 2026", "Daily check: added the Emperor Gateway Conduit (legendary key for the Fallen Emperor on Pendola Pass, crafted from the three ARC couplers or earned at the end of the Frozen Trail Premium pass); Bastions now drop ARC Conductive Coupler; Skulkers also drop ARC Thermo Lining, Heavy Ammo, ARC Coolant, Advanced ARC Powercell and ARC Data Module.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "On phones, rows of filter buttons that scroll sideways now fade at the edge and show an arrow when more buttons are off screen. Tap the arrow or swipe to see them."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Fixes from a full-site check: the Undo button stays usable after an undo; the weapon upgrade planner no longer counts raw materials twice; backups now include map pins, the weekly plan, the squad board and skill builds; ARC Tracker sync no longer unticks quests or empties stash items it could not recognise; adding an item with different capitals no longer makes a duplicate; picking a quest, weapon, enemy or blueprint from search clears filters that would hide it; Share as image downloads the picture if sharing fails; the \"Checked\" date under each tab heading now shows that section's own date; offline, pages you never opened go to the home page instead of loading broken."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Fixes: opening Shopping list, Workshop planner or Shots to kill from Home or search now scrolls to that tool; two starred conditions starting together now each get a notification; Home says when the condition schedule is out of date instead of showing nothing; the server region is now saved in backups; the starred line on Home translates fully; calendar files follow the standard line length."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "The map condition schedule is now checked three times an hour, because GitHub often runs scheduled jobs late or skips them."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Trials helper: each weekly challenge in Reference, Trials now says where to go (map, live condition, enemy sightings or what to bring from your stash), and the week card shows which major condition doubles points right now or next."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Starred map conditions can now notify you when they start (while the site is open in a tab) and can be saved to your phone or computer calendar with a 10-minute reminder."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Raid checklist: the Next raid card on Home lists the items those quests need (ticked when your stash has enough) and the keys you own for that map."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Map condition times now come from the official ARC Raiders map conditions page and follow your server region (picked from your timezone; change it on any map card). The schedule refreshes every hour. The earlier community schedule was wrong on North American servers and missed conditions like Beachcombing and ARC Frigate."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Faster first load: item rows are built as they appear on screen, the Maps tab is only drawn when you open it, and a few slow lookups are cached."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Star any condition on a map card and Home flags it when it starts, with a countdown; until then Home shows when your starred conditions come up next."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "The Next raid card on Home now lists the best live conditions right now: ones that can drop a blueprint on your wishlist, major conditions (Trial points count double), and anything on your next raid map."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Each tab now starts with one short explanation. The yellow how-to box only opens from the How to use button, and the Stash and Gear intros are shorter."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Live map conditions: each map now shows which conditions are on right now with a countdown to when they end, what is coming up next and when, and switches by itself when they change. Home has a Map conditions right now card, and the map list tags each map's current condition. The schedule comes from MetaForge's community feed and is refreshed daily; if your server runs a few hours off, shift the times on the map card."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Cleaner phone layout: long tab intros fold to two lines with a More button, the search box on Recycle and the filters on Stash stay at the top while you scroll, and the More menu has bigger buttons that are easier to tap."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Maps follow your quests: the map your quest route sends you to next gets a star and a Next raid tag, Raid prep has a Show my quest spots on the map button that pins your active quest spots in walking order, and keys are marked You have it or Missing (from your stash, or tick I have it yourself)."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Smarter search: the Search everything box now also finds tools (type a tool name and press Enter to open it), maps, map conditions (like Night Raid, showing which maps get it) and quests that need the item you typed."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Answers right on the item: every item in Recycle now shows a quick verdict (keep it, recycle it or sell it, depending on what your quests, projects, goals and workshop still need and which is worth more coins), a Craft or sell line for craftable items, and which workshop levels you have not built yet still need it."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Tools tab is shorter: tools that do the same job now share one entry. Keep or recycle, Loot value and Stash worth are under What's it worth?; Compare weapons, Shots to kill and Weapon upgrade path are under Weapons; Crafting planner, Shopping list and Workshop planner are under Crafting and shopping. The list went from 22 entries to 16, and every tool still works the same."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Maps now show only the conditions that can happen on that map, taken from each map's wiki page. Before, every map listed every condition, so Beachcombing showed up everywhere even though it only happens on Riven Tides.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "The site now counts how often each tool in the Tools tab is opened and used (anonymous counts only, no cookies or personal data), so tools that hardly anyone uses can be retired later to keep the tab tidy."],
    ["Oct 16, 2026", "Daily check: added the Bully Fragmenter (epic, sells for 5,000 coins, dropped by the Bully and the Courier) and the quest Bait, Fetch, Blast (Apollo, Pendola Pass, after Tracks Of The Beast). Pendola Pass now unlocks after 25 rounds. The Bully now lists its attacks, weak points, drops and Pendola Pass, and the Skulker its attack, XP, weak points and the Skulker Targeter drop. Integrated Binoculars sell for 0 coins (built into the Looting Mk. 3 (Cautious)).", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Added Google's site check file so the site can be listed and tracked in Google Search Console."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "New name: the site is now Speranza Field Guide, so it no longer shares a name with other ARC Raiders sites and Discords. The web address, your saved stash, quests and settings stay the same."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Easier to find and nicer to share: clearer page titles and descriptions for Google, a new link preview image, a full preview card on every item and map page when shared on Discord, Reddit or X, and the sitemap now tells Google when the data last changed."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "The Quests tab now starts on Not completed, so finished quests stay out of the way (pick All quests to see them). With a mouse you can left-click and drag the Quest chain map to move around it."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "New Quest chain map in the Quests tab: every quest laid out step by step in the order they unlock, with lines from each quest to the ones it opens, and done, ready and locked quests marked. Tap a quest or pick one from the list to light up the path to it and see the quests left to finish, in order."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "New Craft or sell tool in Tools: every craftable item with what it sells for next to what its materials sell for, so you can see whether crafting gains coins or you should just sell the materials. It shows how many you can craft from your Stash right now, and the Crafting planner shows the same answer for the item you pick."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Added a security policy on GitHub that explains how to privately report a security problem with the site."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Site changes now shows only the 5 newest changes, so the page stays short. Press Show more to see older ones."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Fixed: on a phone, the first ARC Tracker sync no longer loops on \"Resync to check your first sync\". After Resync the bar says what was found and to press Apply, and scrolls to the Apply button; if ARC Tracker rejects your key, the bar says so too."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Fixed: ARC Tracker sync works again with the site's new ARC Tracker app key. The key box now warns you if you paste an app key (starts with arc_k1_) instead of your own user key (starts with arc_u1_, from ARC Tracker Settings > Developer Access)."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "The daily data check now also works through the Data gaps list every day: anything the wiki has filled in since (a sell price, a source, a key's spot on the map) is added to the site and shows under Wiki updates."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Route on one map: each raid in the Quest route planner, and the Next raid card on Home, has a Show route on map button. It opens the enlarged map with every spot those quests name, numbered in a short walking order and joined by a dashed line, and lists which quest each stop is for."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Loadout cost vs haul: the Raid log in Tools has a Kit value box, or pick a saved loadout to fill it in from sell prices. Each raid then shows its profit (haul minus kit; a death loses the kit), and the raid log and Raids tab show profit per map. The loadout builder and saved loadouts show what each kit is worth."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Fixed the daily item sync trying to put back Apollo's old 6-per-day Noisemaker limit. The wiki's newer answer (no daily limit) is now kept as a wiki override, so the sync leaves it alone."],
    ["Oct 15, 2026", "Daily check: added the quest A Path Not Yours (Nomadic Envoys, The Blue Gate, after Taking Stock). Amplifications now match the wiki's new Amplified Weapons page: Anti Shield is for the Kettle, Bigger Mag adds the Aphelion, More Reload adds the Il Toro, Increased Burst adds the Aphelion, High Velocity now lists its effect, and Straight Bolt is now called Ergonomic Bolt. Apollo no longer limits Noisemaker purchases per day.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 14, 2026", "Filled in data gaps from the wiki: sell prices for 20 items (Calculator, Hand Drill, Steel Cable, Skulker Targeter, Stiletto and more), where to get 27 items (traders, quests, ARC drops, area types and Gunsmith upgrades for Bantam, Stiletto and Rascal tiers), recipes for Bantam I, Stiletto I, Grappling Hook, Yank Grenade and Basic Camera, and map spots for the JKV Employee Access Card (Space Travel) and the Communication Tower Key (Pilgrim's Peak).", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 14, 2026", "New Wiki updates button in the Site changes tab: press it to see only the game data the daily check picked up from the wiki (new quests, items, enemies, trials and fixes), day by day, with the date of the last check."],
    ["Oct 14, 2026", "Daily check: added the new quest Divided (Nomadic Envoys, Pendola Pass, after Ruins And Reverberations). Belly Of The Beast now lists all 7 objectives and needs Tracks Of The Beast too. Bastions also show up on Pendola Pass. Trials moved to Season 6, Week 2 (October 13 to 19) with the new challenges.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Every part of the site's data is now checked daily: recycling and salvage, weapons and gear, enemies, traders, workshop, blueprints, project presets, trials, maps and update history join items, quests, keys, skills and sightings."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "The data date at the top and bottom of the site now shows when the daily check last ran, even on days when nothing changed. The Data freshness table shows both the last check and the last change."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Gear cards now have the same spacing everywhere: even gaps between cards, cards in a row match heights, and the Report button stays next to the name on phones."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Fresh look: the title, buttons and ARC Tracker bar now sit together at the top, cards have soft depth and lift on hover, big numbers use the game-style font, and stat tiles carry the four-colour stripe. The Home Raids card shows what you brought out and your profit, and opens the Raids tab."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Fixed: raids from ARC Tracker now sync with the right time, value brought out, profit and length. Raid cards also show what you brought in and your kills."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "New Raids tab: every raid synced from ARC Tracker or logged by hand, with what you brought out and your profit per raid, totals, extract rate, best raid and a per-map breakdown. Filter by outcome, map and time, and sort by newest, value or profit."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Fixed: the raider level no longer shows as 1. ARC Tracker's API currently sends level 1 instead of your real level, so the site hides it until ARC Tracker sends the right number."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "Fixed: raider level from ARC Tracker is found in more places in your profile, and an old wrong level is cleared when ARC Tracker no longer sends one. The ARC Tracker Settings panel can now show exactly what ARC Tracker sent for your profile, to copy into a bug report."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync now re-checks by itself every few minutes while the site is open and when you come back to the tab, so new data from the ARC Tracker Link app shows up without pressing Resync. It asks for a small check first and only runs the full sync when something changed."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "New look for Maps, Frozen Trail, Updates and Site changes: summary tiles at the top of each, map cards with an edge colored by difficulty (and your raid count and extract rate per map), colored-edge cards for the Frozen Trail sections and each game update, and site changes grouped by day."],
    ["Oct 13, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync moved to a bar at the top of every page, with a Resync button and a Settings button for your key. The Tracker tab is gone: set a Want amount on any Stash card (or when adding an item) to mark a material you are looking for, and use the new Looking for filter. Stash cards also show what each item is used to craft. The Shopping list and Workshop planner moved from Stash to Tools."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "New look for Gear, Reference and Tools: weapons and gear sit in a two-column grid of cards with a rarity-colored edge, enemy cards have an edge colored by threat level, and each tool card has an accent edge. The colored card edges now show properly on Quests too."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Fixed: ARC Tracker sync now copies every item in your stash into the Stash tab, not only items you already had a count for (that was an opt-in box that was off by default)."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "New look for Home, Recycle and Quests, matching the Stash and Tracker tabs: summary tiles at the top of Home and Quests, cards with a colored edge (item rarity on Recycle, open, done or locked on Quests), quieter Tag, Note, Link and Report buttons, and the quest share and code tools tucked into one Share or load progress box."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync now shows your raider level: on a Raider level card at the top of Home and in the sync line on the Stash tab."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "The Tracker tab is now just the materials you are looking for, styled like the Stash tab: add a material and how many you need, then count it up with +1, +5 or +10. The shopping list, workshop planner, ARC Tracker sync and history moved to the Stash tab, and backups and Reset everything moved to Home. Your saved counts did not change."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "ARC Tracker sync now copies everything its API offers: completed quests, stash, workshop station levels, learned blueprints, the stage you are on in each running project, and your raids into the raid log. It syncs by itself every time you open the site after the first sync, which you still check before applying. Skill trees are not in ARC Tracker's API, so they stay manual."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "New Stash tab: every item you have, with its value, split into what to keep (and which quest, workbench or Outpost upgrade, project or tracked material needs it) and what is safe to sell, with the coins and slots that frees. Filter by Sell or Keep, sort by value or slots, and change counts right on the cards. Counts include anything synced from ARC Tracker."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Workshop upgrade path in the Tracker tab: choose to plan the next level, the next two, or every level left. The planner lists those levels in order with how ready you are and what each unlocks, then every item you still need with the ARC enemies that drop it, the area types to search and the best items to recycle. The shopping list follows the same choice."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Enemy sighting reports are now checked every day: once two different people report the same enemy on a map its card does not list, the map is added under Players saw it, and reports already on the card are closed with a thank-you."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Quests now show where to go: quests whose objectives name a place on the map list it under Where, and Show on map opens the enlarged map with each spot marked and numbered by objective."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Quests: added Ruins And Reverberations (Celeste, Pendola Pass, after Wires Crossed), new on the wiki today. Bring a Spotter Relay; rewards are 2 Smoke Grenades, Looting Mk. 3 (Safekeeper), 3 Electrical Components and 2 Speaker Components.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "New Shots to kill tool in the Tools tab: pick an ARC enemy to rank every weapon by how fast it deals that enemy's health (hits, magazines, rough time and armor penetration), or pick one weapon and tier for its numbers. Each enemy card has a Shots to kill button."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Patch notes for you: the Updates tab marks game updates that are new since your last visit and highlights notes that mention the items, quests, blueprints, weapons and maps you track or use. When a new update is out, Home shows a short card about it. No pop-ups."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Enemy sighting reports: every ARC enemy card has a Report a sighting button. Pick the map you saw it on and it opens a short GitHub issue; maps with enough reports show on the card under Players saw it. Your own sightings show on the card and count in the map filter and Raid prep."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "ARC enemy cards in Reference > Enemies: each enemy now shows a threat rating, health, armor, attack, XP, the maps it is seen on, which of its drops you still need, and the quests that involve it. Filter by type, map, or enemies that drop what you need. The Raid prep on the Maps tab lists the ARC seen on that map."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Quests: added Wires Crossed (Celeste, after Exploring Pendola Pass), which is now on the wiki. To The Skies now lists its maps, the four ARC parts you install and its full objectives, and both it and Exploring Pendola Pass now follow Off The Radar. The Data freshness table at the bottom of the site now shows which parts are re-checked every day.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "New Home tab: your next raid from the quest route, the workshop upgrade you are closest to, goals, raid log stats and stash worth on one screen, each with a button to the full tool. Once you have saved progress the site opens on Home; untick the box at the bottom to keep opening on Recycle."],
    ["Oct 12, 2026", "Data checks now run every day: sell prices, weights and recipes are re-checked against the RaidTheory data set daily instead of weekly, and wiki edits to quests, keys and skills are checked daily too, so changes reach the site sooner."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Quest route planner in the Tools tab: groups your active quests into as few raids as possible (busiest map first, any-map quests fill the gaps), lists each quest's objectives and the items they need, and updates as you tick quests off."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Weapon upgrade path tool in the Tools tab: pick a weapon, the tier you have and the tier you want to see every Gunsmith step, the total materials (or basic materials), what your tracker still needs, and add it all to your projects in one tap."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Blueprint wishlist: tick On my wishlist on any blueprint in Reference > Blueprints to get a Blueprint hunt list of which containers, conditions, quests and ARC to go after. The Raid prep on the Maps tab also lists wishlist blueprints you can find on that map. Included in backups."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Share as image now works for your skill build, your loadout and your raid log, as well as materials and quest progress. On a phone it opens the share sheet; on a computer it saves a PNG."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Raid log charts: a bar chart of your last 30 raids (haul value, deaths in red, your average as a dashed line), a bar for each map's extract rate, and how your last 10 raids compare with your overall extract rate."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Stash worth tool in the Tools tab: adds up what everything in your tracker sells for, and lists the spare items (beyond your quests, projects, workshop upgrades and goals) that free the most slots or bring in the most coins. One tap sends the freed slots to the Stash space planner."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Sell price history: the weekly data sync now records every sell price change. Item pages and the item list show when a price last went up or down, and Loot value in the Tools tab has a Price changes list. Recording starts today, so older changes are not listed."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Data gaps list at the top of this tab shows what the site still does not know: items with no known source or sell price, quests with no objectives or rewards, and keys with no source or no spot on the map. Each list has a button to report what you know."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Raid log in the Tools tab: log each raid's map, whether you extracted or died, and your haul value, and see your extract rate, average and best haul per map and your extract streak. It is saved in your browser and included in backups."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Skill build planner is now laid out like the in-game tree: a starting skill, two early paths, the first large node, three middle columns and the final large node. Tap a skill to add a point; skills stay locked until the one before them has a point, and you cannot take out a point that a later skill depends on. The final large node now allows two picks (the first at 30 points, the second at 40), and every skill now shows its max points."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Skill build planner in the Tools tab: spend points across Conditioning, Mobility and Survival, see how many of your 76 level points (plus Expedition bonus points) are left, and share the build as a link. It flags a large node taken before its tree has 10, or 30 to 40, points, or two picks from the same large node. The wiki does not list every skill's max points or which small skill leads to which, so those are marked as assumed and not checked."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Weapon upgrades: the Crafting planner now covers weapon tiers II to IV, counting the lower tier and every upgrade part down to basic materials, and weapons show what each upgrade costs with a Plan this craft link. Fixed upgrade costs that were shown one tier too late (for example, Rattler I to II costs 10 Metal Parts and 10 Rubber Parts, as on the wiki)."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Loot value tool in the Tools tab ranks items by sell price per kilogram or per stash slot (a full stack), so you know what is worth the space in your bag. It notes when recycled parts sell for more, and marks items your active quests, projects, goals or Keep tags still need. Weapons, augments and shields are left out unless you tick the box."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New Crafting planner in the Tools tab: pick any of the 144 craftable items and how many, and it works out every part down to basic materials, uses components your tracker already has, and lists the workbenches you need. Save the result as a project to feed the Tracker shopping list, or copy a link. Items with a recipe now have a Plan this craft link."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Sell prices, weights, recipes and the extra where to find details are now re-checked against the RaidTheory data set every week, so they keep up with game patches. Each refresh adds a line here listing what changed."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Quests: a new Next up list shows the quests you can start right now and what each one still needs from your Tracker, closest to ready first. It follows the trader and map filters, and items you only pick up during a quest are listed separately. Fixed Exploring Pendola Pass asking for \"Wire\" instead of Wires."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Keys: every key now says how to get it, from its wiki page and the quest data. 8 keys are quest rewards (up from 2), the Blue Gate security codes name the area to search, and a few keys name the containers they drop from. Each map has a Keys list with a button that shows the door on the map.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Where to find items: 205 items gained details the wiki was missing, such as area types (85 items), traders with price and daily limit (28), and how to get weapon tiers II to IV by upgrading at the Gunsmith, with the upgrade cost. Items with no source at all dropped from 190 to 27. The extra details come from RaidTheory/arcraiders-data and only fill gaps the wiki leaves.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Faster loading: the site now downloads only the language you use (English visitors skip about 320 KB of translations), draws the item list in batches so the page appears sooner, and builds the Gear tab when you open it."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Items now show their sell price, weight and stack size, the recipe and workbench if you can craft them, and what they are used to craft. Each item also says what its recycled or salvaged parts sell for, so you can see when recycling beats selling. The lookup can sort by sell price, and item pages and api/v1/items.json carry the same numbers. Prices, weights and recipes come from RaidTheory/arcraiders-data (MIT) and were spot-checked against the wiki."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Phones: the bottom bar now fits Recycle, Tracker, Quests and Maps plus a More menu for the other tabs, and the header is shorter so the page content starts higher up."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "New logo: the whole triangle is made of the four colours, in equal parts around its sides."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "The colour stripes at the top of the site and in the logo now run blue, green, yellow, red."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Added the five Amplification Modules (Mk. I to V) with where they drop, and a new Amplification section in Reference listing every weapon upgrade, its effect, research project and compatible weapons. Search everything finds both. The Mk. I wiki page would not load, so its details follow the other four."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Backups: new Download file and Import from file buttons. The backup file is versioned and includes item and quest IDs, and importing understands IDs as well as names. New read-only data files for items, quests, maps and keys are published under api/v1/ with stable IDs."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Search everything now finds keys and keycards (from the wiki key list). Pick one to open the detailed map at the building it opens, with the wiki wording for the floor or corner. Type key and a map name to list that map's keys."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Search everything: type a loot type and a map together (for example industrial spaceport or nature dam) to list the matching rooms on that map."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Search everything now finds loot area types (Industrial, Electrical, Nature, Technological and so on, also electronic or plants). Pick one to see its rooms on every map and the items the wiki lists for it."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Recycle: the partial tag on an item is now a button. Press it to see why the item is marked partial."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Search everything now finds map rooms by name or by area type (Industrial, Electrical, Medical and so on) and opens the detailed map at that room."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Recycle: removed the long note under the filters that listed the wiki pages loaded and explained the partial badge."],
    ["Oct 11, 2026", "Mobile: a much more compact header, and the filter and tab rows now scroll sideways in one line instead of wrapping into many rows. Feedback moved into the Display menu on phones."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Quests: checked every quest's order against the wiki and fixed the Celeste chain (A Balanced Harvest, Untended Garden, After Rain Comes, The Root Of The Matter, Celeste's Journals, The Major's Footlocker, Water Troubles, Back On Top). Added Belly Of The Beast and Tracks Of The Beast. The quest list is now sorted so a quest always comes after the ones you need first.", "wiki"],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Fixed Celeste's Childhood Drawings showing as unlocked: it now requires Shoring Up Defenses first."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Quests: a new button marks a quest and every quest before it as done in one go, with an extra press to confirm and an Undo."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Where to farm this now covers the plants: Lemon, Apricot, Prickly Pear, Olives, Mushroom, Great Mullein and Fruit Mix, with the trees, cacti and baskets they come from."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "The Tracker now accepts any item in the game, not just materials, and every tracked entry has +1 / +5 / +10 and Where to farm this."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Removed the Where do I farm this? tool from Tools. Where to farm this is still on every shopping list row."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "New logo in the header, a Display menu (raid mode, text size, reduced motion, theme and contrast), +1 / +5 / +10 buttons on the shopping list, +1 to tracker in search, map layers by room type, route lines through your pins and shareable map views."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "New tools: Pre-raid planner, Weekly goals and Squad board. Added keyboard shortcuts (press ?), a What is new pop-up, an offline badge, a Credits section and a page for every item that search engines can find."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "The quick tour now has 11 steps covering the shopping list, Where to farm this, reset, tool tabs, map search and the enlarged map, Site changes and languages."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added German, Italian, Russian and Chinese translations. Where to farm this now shows wiki sources for about 190 items: area types, matching places on the maps, ARC enemy drops, traders and quests."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Tools are now split into sub-tabs, one tool at a time, instead of one long list."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "The shopping list's Find items button is now Where to farm this: the area types the wiki lists for each material, plus matching places on each map you can open. The Farm finder tool shows the same. Area types come from the wiki's Can Be Found In lists; places are matched using the in-game map icons."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a Reset everything to default button in the Tracker that clears quests, tracker, goals, projects, checklists, notes, pins and loadouts back to zero. It keeps language, theme and contrast."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Site changes now have their own tab (this one)."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Updated the maps data freshness and styled the room finder."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a map viewer upgrade: zoom and pan on the enlarged map, a room finder across all maps, personal pins saved on your device, and links that preview the map when shared. Also added a squad checklist link, a Link button on items, and search pages for each map."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Improved the link preview image and search tags (a sitemap and robots file for search engines)."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a tip to the Maps how-to explaining that an enlarged map has much more detail."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added detailed, zoomable maps for 7 maps with a key and 115 named rooms, from in-game screenshots. Difficulty and unlock data were not re-checked."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added Japanese, French and Spanish translations, with a button to report translation errors on GitHub. Also added a phone tab bar, reset countdowns, a farm finder, a stash planner, sell/keep hints, a recycle sort and rarity filter, an install button and per-tab Checked dates."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Phone fixes: item action buttons now sit in one row below the name, and the + Cart button is hidden so rows no longer overlap."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added Undo, a first-visit tour, a trials tracker, item notes, a quest map filter, raid prep, a history chart, shared shopping list links, a sound cue and accessibility fixes."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Tracker cards and the shopping list now take typed counts in a box instead of plus and minus buttons, and keep rows in a stable order."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Moved the shopping list and workshop planner into the Tracker tab. Quest and workshop needs are tracked automatically, with an optional auto-subtract when you complete something."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added Trials (Season 6) to the Reference tab: how Trials work, the Week 1 challenges and removed challenges. Point values and season rewards are not on the wiki yet. Also fixed selected chips going blank on hover."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a workshop planner, shopping list, daily and weekly tasks, item tags, map notes, saved loadouts, a high-contrast mode, a print view, quest share codes and Research Station levels 1 to 4 (a stub: crafting details are not published yet)."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a quiet Ko-fi link in the footer."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added global search, a keep/recycle list, share-as-image, loadout links, an offline indicator, a new-update dot, a feedback button and a Sheltered Retreat project preset from a community guide (the wiki page would not load)."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Redid the social preview image and app icons in the ARC Raiders palette."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Recolored the whole site to the ARC Raiders palette: black and cream with red, yellow, green and cyan stripes."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Visual cleanup: shorter tab names, a tidier Quests toolbar, boxed Tools sections and shorter hints and intros."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added quest planning (goals, sorting, a to-do link and a recycle warning), weapon compare, a loadout builder, a transfer code with snapshots, and data freshness notes."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added a Reference tab with enemies, traders, workshop upgrades, skills and a blueprint tracker."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Quests are now hidden until the previous quest in the wiki quest chain is completed, with an optional show-locked toggle."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Quests can be marked completed, with a completion filter and a progress count. Completion is included in backups."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added objectives for all 107 quests, and made them searchable."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Added the Quests tab with 107 quests and wiki project presets for the Project helper."],
    ["Oct 10, 2026", "Gear now shows rarity, weight and sell prices, plus grenade damage and sorting for grenades and augments. Removed the Aphelion stars."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added the Weapons & gear tab with stats from the wiki."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added the Tools tab, favorites, a cart, fuzzy search, backup and restore, offline support and a contributing guide."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Tap or click a map to open an enlarged, zoomable view."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added a How to use button with a hint for each tab."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added goals, shareable links, a theme toggle, a first-time hint, a keyboard shortcut, an app manifest, a social preview image and an issue template."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added GoatCounter, a simple visitor counter."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added map images for all the maps, shown in full without cropping."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Added the Maps tab with a card for each map."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Expanded the update history with highlights for each update."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Wrong-number reports now go to GitHub Issues."],
    ["Oct 9, 2026", "Rebuilt the site: all 238 items from the wiki material pages, a recycle/salvage toggle, a materials tracker and a Frozen Trail 2.0 summary."]
  ];
